WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.478
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.083
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:17.330
Unit four: Part 2: Wh- Questions. Today you will answer who, what, when, where, why and how questions quickly.

4
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.363
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.614
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.556
Question word.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.782
Question word means a word like who or where.

8
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.069
Listen to the first word.

9
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:35.243
Your turn. Say: Question word.

10
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.298
Question word.

11
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.179
Response.

12
00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:44.136
Response means an answer.

13
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.657
Choose the best response.

14
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.274
Your turn. Say: Response.

15
00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.320
Response.

16
00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:55.910
Appointment.

17
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:59.415
Appointment means an arranged meeting time.

18
00:01:00.017 --> 00:01:01.714
I have an appointment at three.

19
00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:04.551
Your turn. Say: Appointment.

20
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.389
Appointment.

21
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.058
Deadline.

22
00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:13.711
Deadline means the last time to finish something.

23
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:15.852
The deadline is Friday.

24
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.928
Your turn. Say: Deadline.

25
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:22.861
Deadline.

26
00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:24.757
Supervisor.

27
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.539
Supervisor means a person who manages workers.

28
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.778
Ask your supervisor.

29
00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:34.454
Your turn. Say: Supervisor.

30
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.406
Supervisor.

31
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.186
Reception.

32
00:01:41.183 --> 00:01:43.949
Reception means the desk where visitors arrive.

33
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.899
Go to reception.

34
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:49.287
Your turn. Say: Reception.

35
00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.274
Reception.

36
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:54.936
Confirm.

37
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.402
Confirm means to say that something is certain.

38
00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:00.505
I will confirm the booking.

39
00:02:01.117 --> 00:02:03.572
Your turn. Say: Confirm.

40
00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:07.353
Confirm.

41
00:02:08.117 --> 00:02:09.280
Similar sound.

42
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:13.688
Similar sound means words that sound alike but differ in meaning.

43
00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:16.132
Beware of similar sounds.

44
00:02:16.717 --> 00:02:19.137
Your turn. Say: Similar sound.

45
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.001
Similar sound.

46
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.207
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.166
Visal, how does Part 2 work?

48
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:41.368
You hear a question or statement and three responses, and you choose the best response. Nothing is printed, so you must listen to the first words carefully.

49
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:45.075
What is the key skill with Wh- questions?

50
00:02:46.183 --> 00:02:55.720
Identify the question word. Who needs a person, when needs a time, where needs a place, why needs a reason, and how many needs a number.

51
00:02:56.817 --> 00:02:58.468
What are common traps?

52
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:09.155
A wrong answer may repeat a word from the question with a different meaning, such as a similar sound. Yes and No do not answer Wh- questions.

53
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.951
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:17.846
Grammar focus: Strategy: hear the question word, predict the answer type.

55
00:03:18.146 --> 00:03:19.275
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:23.216
Who is in charge of the project? Ms. Park is.

57
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:27.059
When is the deadline? By Friday afternoon.

58
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:35.459
Listen carefully to the first words and decide what kind of answer is needed. Reject options that only repeat words or answer Yes or No.

59
00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:40.451
Be careful! Don't say: I answer 'When?' with a place.

60
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.959
Say: I answer 'When?' with a time.

61
00:03:45.259 --> 00:03:46.946
Match the question word.

62
00:03:47.733 --> 00:03:50.455
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:52.837
Questions at Reception.

64
00:03:53.137 --> 00:03:56.042
A visitor asks, Where is the sales department?

65
00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.439
The correct reply is, On the third floor.

66
00:04:00.433 --> 00:04:02.352
Another asks, When is the meeting?

67
00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:06.910
A wrong option repeats the word meeting but does not say a time.

68
00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.969
The best reply is, At ten o'clock.

69
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:15.196
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.980
Part 2 has blank responses.

71
00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.121
A, two. B, three. C, four.

72
00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.237
The answer is B: three.

73
00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:29.313
'When' needs an answer about blank.

74
00:04:29.613 --> 00:04:33.162
A, a person. B, a place. C, time.

75
00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.409
The answer is C: time.

76
00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.026
Yes and No blank Wh- questions.

77
00:04:42.326 --> 00:04:46.966
A, do not answer. B, always answer. C, are required for.

78
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.883
The answer is A: do not answer.

79
00:04:54.017 --> 00:04:55.656
Where is the sales department?

80
00:04:55.956 --> 00:05:00.643
A, Ms. Park. B, on the third floor. C, at ten o'clock.

81
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.583
The answer is B: on the third floor.

82
00:05:07.717 --> 00:05:09.728
A wrong option often blank.

83
00:05:10.028 --> 00:05:14.656
A, is very long. B, is a number. C, repeats a word.

84
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.687
The answer is C: repeats a word.

85
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.994
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.604
How do you answer a Wh- question in Part 2?

87
00:05:37.417 --> 00:05:39.033
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:53.981
I listen to the first words to find the question word. Then I predict the type of answer, such as a person, a time or a place. I choose the response that matches, and I reject answers that only repeat words.

89
00:05:54.281 --> 00:05:55.921
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:56.817 --> 00:06:02.894
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: hear the question word, predict the answer type.

91
00:06:03.194 --> 00:06:07.007
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:06:07.307 --> 00:06:09.576
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

93
00:06:09.876 --> 00:06:12.401
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

